+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+Tool definitions supply the JSON Schema sent to providers. The registry applies that same schema to each tool call before an executor receives input.
+
+## Contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` describing a failed required, type, or enum constraint, including the failing property path and constraint but no input value; it does not invoke the executor or log input values ([validated by: rejects malformed input without executing or exposing values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L15)).
+- Schema-valid input, including unlisted properties, reaches the executor unchanged exactly once; a static schema is compiled at registration and reused for later calls ([validated by: passes valid input unchanged after validating against the registered schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L47)).
+- Registration rejects an uncompilable static schema immediately and names its tool ([validated by: rejects a broken static schema at registration](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L74)).
+- A function-valued definition uses the schema resolved for each execution ([validated by: validates each dynamic definition against its current schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L81)).
+- A rejected tool call becomes a tool result the provider can read on its next round, allowing a corrected retry within the configured tool-round bound ([validated by: returns validation feedback to the provider for a corrected retry](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L7)).
+- An unregistered tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` ([validated by: rejects malformed input without executing or exposing values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L15)).
